        },
        {
          "type": "intro",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "intro"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "section-inner editorial-split"
              },
              "html": "<div><p class=\"section-label\">Relationship anniversary</p><h2 class=\"section-title\">Your own date, all year round</h2></div><div class=\"intent-prose\"><p>At first, you count the months. Years later, you may find yourselves booking the same table again. Start this anniversary with something specific: your first conversation, the film you didn’t really watch that night or the meal you shared when you met.</p><p>Whether you are marking a dating, civil partnership or wedding anniversary, a big surprise is optional. Decide together what you want to celebrate and make some time for each other.</p><h3>Wedding anniversary gifts for one, five or twenty years</h3><p>Choose a specific memory from the past year and something you would like to share in the next. Recreate a dish from your wedding, open a photo album and exchange a few handwritten lines. For a gift to experience rather than unwrap, suggest an evening you plan together, with a Caresse audio discovery if the format appeals to you.</p><h3>A civil partnership anniversary at home</h3><p>Start with the day you registered your partnership or a memory of your first home together. Prepare a simple dinner, choose a song from that time and leave room to talk about what you would like to share this year. Keep surprises in the details of the evening; choose any intimate activity together.</p><h3>Dating anniversary ideas: revisit your first date</h3><p>Bring back the food, music or film from the start of your story, then add something that reflects you today. A small budget or same-day preparation can still make the occasion personal. If you choose Caresse, hear a free demo first; creating audio fiction from your preferences then uses a paid credit.</p></div>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "container",
          "tag": "section",
          "attrs": {
            "class": "ideas-section"
          },
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "container",
              "tag": "div",
              "attrs": {
                "class": "section-inner"
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "container",
                  "tag": "div",
                  "attrs": {
                    "class": "ideas-heading"
                  },
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "type": "element",
                      "tag": "p",
                      "attrs": {
                        "class": "section-label"
                      },
                      "html": "Relationship anniversary"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "element",
                      "tag": "h2",
                      "attrs": {
                        "class": "section-title"
                      },
                      "html": "Five ways to celebrate your story"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "element",
                  "tag": "ol",
                  "attrs": {
                    "class": "ideas-grid"
                  },
                  "html": "<li class=\"idea-card \"><div class=\"idea-top\"><span class=\"idea-number\">01 / 05</span></div><h3>Recreate your first date at home</h3><p>Cook the dish you had that night, put on the film you didn’t really watch that night or tell each other what you first thought. You could even imagine a new ending to that first date.</p></li><li class=\"idea-card \"><div class=\"idea-top\"><span class=\"idea-number\">02 / 05</span></div><h3>Write about what you love today</h3><p>Share a few lines: a memory from this year, a small gesture you appreciate and something you would like to do next. A personal letter can sit beside dinner without replacing the conversation.</p></li><li class=\"idea-card \"><div class=\"idea-top\"><span class=\"idea-number\">03 / 05</span></div><h3>Plan a surprise together</h3><p>One of you chooses dinner; the other picks music or dessert. Agree on a budget and mood together, and leave the small details as a surprise.</p></li><li class=\"idea-card featured\"><div class=\"idea-top\"><span class=\"idea-number\">04 / 05</span></div><h3>Share a Caresse experience</h3><p>After looking back, share a moment in the present. Try a free audio demo in the app, then decide whether to create an intimate guided fiction based on your preferences. Personalisation uses a paid credit, with no subscription.</p></li><li class=\"idea-card wide\"><div class=\"idea-top\"><span class=\"idea-number\">05 / 05</span></div><h3>Leave with another date in the diary</h3><p>Choose something small to do before your next anniversary: a walk, breakfast together or an evening without notifications. Pick a date that actually works for both of you.</p></li>"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
